T*
(Executive Summary) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Admin access has a strong base: non-super-admin users are pinned to their own organization by) Tj
T*
(backend middleware, suspended organizations are blocked at authentication time, most tenant) Tj
T*
(write routes are subscription-gated, and Admin role permissions are generally narrower than) Tj
T*
(Super Admin permissions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The highest risk is not broad Admin access across organizations. The highest risk is data) Tj
T*
(integrity inside the Admin organization. Admins can currently delete converted leads, and) Tj
T*
(prospects are hard-deleted even when they are terminal WON or LOST. Because customers are) Tj
T*
(derived from Prospect.stage === WON, these delete paths can damage customer lineage, reports,) Tj
T*
(and historical CRM data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The second major risk is API-side validation and authorization drift. The Leads API accepts a) Tj
T*
(raw productInterested item id without confirming that the item belongs to the same organization.) Tj
T*
(The Profile API accepts organization PDF asset uploads from any authenticated organization user) Tj
T*
(if they craft the request, even though the UI only exposes this to Admin and Manager.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
