(- Admin has backend permissions for users, items, leads, prospects, quotations, reports, audit) Tj
T*
(read, announcements, billing read, dashboard read, and organization read/update.) Tj
T*
(- Admin cannot create Admin users through the backend permission utility; Admin can create) Tj
T*
(Manager and Executive users.) Tj
T*
(- Super Admin-only password reset is enforced in userService.resetUserPassword, even though the) Tj
T*
(route uses a broader USER_UPDATE permission.) Tj
T*
(- Admin dashboard route additionally enforces exact role match.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Issues:) Tj
T*
(- Some sensitive capabilities rely on frontend hiding rather than backend authorization. The) Tj
T*
(clearest example is Profile organization asset upload.) Tj
T*
(- Admin-visible Help still says Admin can reset user passwords, but backend restricts this to) Tj
T*
(Super Admin.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Best-practice solution:) Tj
T*
(- Treat frontend role checks as UX only.) Tj
T*
(- Add backend permission checks for every role-sensitive file field and workflow action.) Tj
T*
(- Maintain a role capability matrix and test it at API level for Admin, Manager, Executive, and) Tj
T*
(Super Admin.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Organization Data Isolation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Observed:) Tj
T*
(- requireOrganization pins every non-super-admin request to req.user.organizationId.) Tj
T*
(- Core tenant modules query by organizationId.) Tj
T*
(- Suspended organizations are blocked in requireAuth.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Issues:) Tj
T*
(- Lead productInterested is connected by item id without validating the item belongs to the same) Tj
T*
(organization.) Tj
T*
(- Prospect and quotation flows validate many related records correctly, but Lead item relation) Tj
T*
(is a gap.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Best-practice solution:) Tj
T*
(- Validate every foreign key relation with { id, organizationId, deletedAt: null } before) Tj
T*
(connecting it.) Tj
T*
(- Prefer composite constraints or service-level guards for cross-organization-sensitive) Tj
T*
(relations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Subscription and Plan Restrictions) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Observed:) Tj
T*
(- Writes in Users, Items, Leads, Prospects, and Quotations are blocked when a subscription is) Tj
T*
(read-only.) Tj
T*
(- Dashboard, Reports, Billing, Audit, notification feed, and announcement feed stay readable for) Tj
T*
(lapsed tenants.) Tj
T*
(- Feature toggles gate announcement authoring and audit-log access.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Issues:) Tj
T*
(- Subscription checks fail open when an organization has no subscription. This is documented as) Tj
T*
(a migration/backfill safety path, but it means a stranded Admin can continue writing.) Tj
T*
(- Quotation PDF is client-rendered, so the QUOTATION_PDF feature is effectively a UI gate.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Best-practice solution:) Tj
T*
(- Monitor and alert on SUBSCRIPTION_MISSING.) Tj
T*
(- Add a startup/backfill invariant that every active organization has a subscription.) Tj
T*
(- For premium client-rendered features, ensure no server-side asset/export endpoint can bypass) Tj
T*
(the plan.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
